<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Flemish region to list GIMV holding.</title>
<headline>Belgian Flemish region to list GIMV holding.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian regional government of Flanders said in a statement on Tuesday it plans to list 15 percent of the shares of its public holding company  GIMV.</p>
<p>It said the expected four billion francs worth of proceeds of the partial listing would be invested in public works.</p>
<p>It gave no time frame for the listing.</p>
<p>The listing will reduce the Flemish government's stake in GIMV to about 70 percent.</p>
